WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:04.570
From his humble start as a stand-out performer
in the '90s sketch comedy show In Living Color,

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:07.560
Jim Carrey has been one of the hottest comedians
in Hollywood.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:12.200
With memorable starring roles in Ace Ventura,
The Mask, Batman Forever, and Dumb &amp; Dumber...

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.520
"Wanna hear the most annoying sound in the
world?

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.000
Ahhh!"

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.060
...Carrey proved himself as one of the best
physical comedians of the 1990s.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:25.680
Even his turns in dramatic roles, like The
Truman Show and Eternal Sunshine of the Spotless

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.120
Mind were met with huge critical success.

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:32.349
But whether you've enjoyed him in big-budget
comedies or surreal dramas, for some reason

00:00:32.349 --> 00:00:36.190
he's been seen on screen less and less in
recent years.

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:40.079
So, why won't Hollywood won't cast Jim Carrey
anymore?

00:00:40.079 --> 00:00:41.859
Box office confusion

00:00:41.859 --> 00:00:46.010
Back in the day, Carrey's films were surefire
box office hits, but his more recent films

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:47.589
have been less of a guarantee.

00:00:47.589 --> 00:00:51.289
His more critically acclaimed films don't
make a ton of money, and his most profitable

00:00:51.289 --> 00:00:53.120
films aren't very well-loved.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:57.100
While Dumb and Dumber To performed well at
the box office, earning about $130 million

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.829
over its budget, reviews were unkind.

00:00:59.829 --> 00:01:04.670
And non-franchise films, like The Incredible
Burt Wonderstone and I Love You Phillip Morris,

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:09.811
weren't financially successful, with Wonderstone
losing $3 million amid negative reviews, and

00:01:09.811 --> 00:01:15.159
Phillip Morris only making a $7 million profit,
despite largely positive reviews.

00:01:15.159 --> 00:01:18.750
Studios want a star with a predictable box
office draw before betting on a big-budget

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:19.750
film.

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:23.340
Despite his talents, no one can be sure if
the next Carrey film will lay an egg.

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:25.090
He's not winning awards

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:29.600
By the early 2000s, Carrey earned four Golden
Globe nominations and two wins in a short

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:30.600
period of time…

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:35.060
"You know, when I go to sleep at night, I'm
not just a guy going to sleep.

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:40.830
I'm two-time Golden Globe winner Jim Carrey
going to get some well-needed shut-eye."

00:01:41.159 --> 00:01:46.179
But unfortunately, he hasn't been nominated
for a major award since 2004's Eternal Sunshine

00:01:46.179 --> 00:01:47.450
of the Spotless Mind.

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:50.969
And even though there was some critical buzz
for I Love You Phillip Morris, he missed out

00:01:50.969 --> 00:01:53.290
on all the major ceremonies.

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:57.820
Carrey's biggest major awards recognition
since then was a Razzie nomination for worst

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:00.040
actor in The Number 23.

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:04.270
Razzie-winning actors have turned it around
before, but they're not always exactly what

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:06.460
casting directors are looking for.

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:08.280
Controversial beliefs

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:12.330
Since his relationship with Jenny McCarthy,
Carrey has been vocal about his stance on

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:16.630
vaccines, which he's called "poison," and
referred to pro-vaccine California governor

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:19.900
Jerry Brown as a "corporate fascist" who "must
be stopped."

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:23.590
While he's entitled to his personal beliefs,
it can be risky for a studio to go with an

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:28.129
actor who could alienate audiences with his
political comments, especially those relating

00:02:28.129 --> 00:02:29.379
to public health.

00:02:29.379 --> 00:02:35.040
In addition to that, Carrey spoke out against
his own film, Kick Ass 2, in 2013, after coming

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:38.750
to the realization that the ultra-violent
comic movie made him uncomfortable because

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:40.160
of recent school shootings.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:44.890
Again, speaking out for your beliefs admirable,
but this particular stand wasn't something

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:48.160
that the studio's promotional tour managers
probably wanted to hear.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:51.780
It wouldn't be surprising if other studios
took notice.

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:53.129
Lawsuit trouble

00:02:53.129 --> 00:02:57.080
As of the making of this video, Carrey is
fighting against wrongful death suits filed

00:02:57.080 --> 00:03:01.530
by the mother and ex-husband of his former
girlfriend Cathriona White, who died of an

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:04.209
intentional drug overdose in 2015.

00:03:04.209 --> 00:03:09.950
White's family alleges that Carrey knowingly
gave their daughter sexually transmitted diseases,

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:14.700
lied to her, threatened her, gave her the
drugs she overdosed on, and then broke up

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:16.590
with her to protect his public image.

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:18.590
Carrey responded in a statement, saying,

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:23.189
"I will not tolerate this heartless attempt
to exploit me or the woman I loved."

00:03:23.189 --> 00:03:28.430
He further called the allegations "irrelevant,
false and improper," and a "shameless shakedown

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:29.430
for money."

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:33.319
It's entirely possible that Carey's free time
might be getting sucked up by dealing with

00:03:33.319 --> 00:03:36.099
putting these lawsuit issues behind him.

00:03:36.099 --> 00:03:37.519
Behind the camera

00:03:37.519 --> 00:03:41.750
More recently, Carrey has been spending more
time behind the camera, working as the creator

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:45.360
and executive producer of the Showtime series
I'm Dying Up Here.

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:49.450
The series draws from Carrey's experiences
as a stand-up comic, starring Melissa Leo

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:52.460
as the owner of a comedy club in the 1970s.

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:56.360
Carrey doesn't act in the show, but he's been
actively promoting the project and working

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:57.739
on it behind the scenes.

00:03:57.739 --> 00:04:01.590
And Carrey seems like he's pretty happy with
life away from the spotlight, saying during

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:05.019
a press panel at the Television Critics Association
that he's...

00:04:05.019 --> 00:04:09.079
"...in the process of shedding layers of persona
at this time in my life.

00:04:09.079 --> 00:04:12.760
… I'm very happy to [be] here for these
guys and watch these guys enter this world

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:14.909
and create these characters."

00:04:14.909 --> 00:04:16.829
How he can turn it around

00:04:16.829 --> 00:04:20.880
For Carrey, the secret to turning his career
around could lie in returning to the small

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:21.880
screen.

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:24.800
His appearance on 30 Rock and The Office made
waves...

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:25.800
"I want the job.

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:27.229
I really do.

00:04:27.229 --> 00:04:30.039
It's just the rest of my family is in the
Finger Lakes right now.

00:04:30.039 --> 00:04:31.879
I'm supposed to be in the Finger Lakes right
now."

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:35.880
...so it's clear that if he doesn't have the
box-office bang required to sell a blockbuster

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:40.280
anymore, there's plenty of room to return
to TV, where he could be a big fish in a smaller

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:41.280
pond.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:44.199
Who wouldn't want to see Jim Carrey in a regular
role on TV again?

00:04:44.199 --> 00:04:48.750
Like many stars, a hit show could help revitalize
his career, and maybe even lead him back to

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:49.940
bigger movie roles in the future.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:51.600
"Hey!

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:52.100
Take a leap, pal."

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:55.040
"THAT'S THE SPIRIT!"

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:56.090
Thanks for watching!

00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:58.560
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:00.530
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

